---
export const prerender = false;
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { resolveLang } from '../lib/i18n';

const lang = resolveLang(Astro);

const copy = {
  zh: {
    title: '圣言诵读：让经文慢下来',
    tagline: '一种古老的读经方式 · 默想而非占卜',
    description: 'Lectio 如何以 Lectio Divina（圣言诵读）的四个步骤陪你读经：诵读、默想、祈祷、默观。',
    intro: 'Lectio 是一种缓慢读经的练习。Lectio Divina（圣言诵读）源自六世纪的本笃会传统，它不追问经文"预示了什么"，而是问"此刻这段话在我身上唤起了什么"。你带着一个真实的问题而来，领受一段经文，然后停留在它里面——在事业、关系、身心健康与信心这些真正要紧的地方，让经文慢慢做工。',
    s1: '一句话概括',
    s1body: '经文提供话语，Lectio Divina 提供停留其中的方法。你不是在解码一条讯息，而是在一段熟悉或陌生的经文前坐下，直到有什么开始回应你。',
    s2: '这个练习的两面',
    s2aTitle: '经文带来话语',
    s2a: '一段不由你挑选的经文。正因为不是你自己选的，它才可能说出你原本不会对自己说的话。诗篇里的哀歌、先知书里的应许、福音书里的一次遇见——每一段都比一句格言更宽，宽到能容下你此刻真实的处境。',
    s2bTitle: 'Lectio Divina 带来节奏',
    s2b: '四个古老的动作：诵读（Lectio）、默想（Meditatio）、祈祷（Oratio）、默观（Contemplatio）。它刻意地慢——重读、停顿、沉默。这里没有需要抢答的问题，也没有需要得出的结论。',
    s3: '四个动作',
    m1Title: '诵读 Lectio — 读',
    m1: '缓慢地读，最好读出声。不急着理解，先让文字经过耳朵。留意哪一个词或哪一句忽然亮起来——那个"绊住你"的地方，就是今天的入口。',
    m2Title: '默想 Meditatio — 想',
    m2: '停在那个词上，反复咀嚼。它让你想起什么？它触到了你生活里的哪一处？不必求出正确解释；这一步问的不是"这段话是什么意思"，而是"它对现在的我说了什么"。',
    m3Title: '祈祷 Oratio — 应',
    m3: '把浮现的东西说回去——感谢、疑问、抗议、恳求都算。这不是表演虔诚，而是诚实。一段没有引起任何回应的读经，还没有读完。',
    m4Title: '默观 Contemplatio — 息',
    m4: '停下言语，只是安静地待着。这一步没有任务，也没有产出。很多人觉得它最难，也最重要——它把读经从一件"做完的事"变成一段被给予的时间。',
    s4: '一次诵读如何进行',
    step1Title: '带一个真实的问题来',
    step1: '不是抽象的神学问题，而是此刻真正压在心上的事：一段关系、一个决定、一种疲惫。',
    step2Title: '领受经文',
    step2: '经文随机而来，不由你挑选。这不是抽签问卜——正因为不是你选的，它才有机会绕过你的预设。',
    step3Title: '慢读，再读一遍',
    step3: '把整章的上下文一起读，而不只是被摘出的那一节。留意哪个词停住了你。',
    step4Title: '默想与回应',
    step4: '让那个词与你的问题相遇。写下、说出、或只在心里回应——诚实比正确重要。',
    step5Title: '安静片刻',
    step5: '合上文字，什么也不做。三十秒也好，十分钟也好。',
    step6Title: '带走一件事',
    step6: '一句要记住的话、一个要打的电话、一次要放下的执着。默想落回生活，才算完成。',
    s5: '经文落在哪里',
    thArea: '人生领域',
    thImagery: '常见经文',
    thRehearse: '默想带来什么',
    row1: ['事业与呼召', '传道书 3:1、腓立比书 4:13、箴言 16:9', '在不确定里分辨下一步，而不是求一个保证'],
    row2: ['关系', '哥林多前书 13:4-7、以弗所书 4:32、罗马书 12:18', '在冲突里先看见自己的那一半'],
    row3: ['身心健康', '马太福音 11:28、诗篇 23、以赛亚书 40:31', '允许自己休息，把疲惫说出口'],
    row4: ['信心与疑惑', '诗篇 13、马可福音 9:24、罗马书 8:28', '把疑问带进祷告，而不是留在门外'],
    s6: '为什么"不是占卜"很重要',
    h1Title: '经文不预言你的未来。',
    h1Body: 'Lectio Divina 从不宣称能揭示将要发生的事。它做的是另一件事：让你在已经发生的事情面前，站得更稳一点。',
    h2Title: '你的回应才是这段时间的重点。',
    h2Body: '没有需要被专家解开的密码。经文摆在那里，重要的是你怎样回应它——这一步没有人能代替你做。',
    h3Title: '这是一个古老而公开的传统。',
    h3Body: 'Lectio Divina 有一千五百年的历史，方法完全公开，任何人都可以自己练习。这里的 AI 只是一个陪伴者：它帮你把问题问得更慢，不替你听见什么。',
    cta: '感受这个练习最自然的方式，就是亲自试一次。带着一个真正重要的问题开始——把出现的经文当作一段可以久坐的话，而不是一个答案。',
    ctaButton: '开始一次诵读',
  },
  en: {
    title: 'Lectio Divina: Reading Scripture Slowly',
    tagline: 'An ancient way of reading \u00b7 reflection, not prediction',
    description: 'How Lectio uses the four movements of Lectio Divina \u2014 read, reflect, respond, rest \u2014 to sit with a passage of scripture.',
    intro: 'Lectio is a practice of reading slowly. Lectio Divina, which comes down to us from the sixth-century Benedictine tradition, never asks what a passage predicts. It asks what this passage stirs in you right now. You arrive with a real question, receive a passage, and stay inside it \u2014 letting it do its work in the places that actually matter: work, relationships, well-being, and faith.',
    s1: 'One idea holds it together',
    s1body: 'Scripture supplies the words; Lectio Divina supplies the way of staying with them. You are not decoding a message. You are sitting down in front of a passage \u2014 familiar or strange \u2014 until something in it begins to answer back.',
    s2: 'The two halves of the practice',
    s2aTitle: 'Scripture brings the words',
    s2a: 'A passage you did not choose. Precisely because you did not pick it, it can say something you would not have said to yourself. A lament from the Psalms, a promise from the prophets, an encounter in the Gospels \u2014 each is wider than a maxim, wide enough to hold whatever you actually walked in with.',
    s2bTitle: 'Lectio Divina brings the rhythm',
    s2b: 'Four old movements: Lectio (read), Meditatio (reflect), Oratio (respond), Contemplatio (rest). It is deliberately slow \u2014 rereading, pausing, silence. There is no question to answer quickly here, and no conclusion you are required to reach.',
    s3: 'The four movements',
    m1Title: 'Lectio \u2014 Read',
    m1: 'Read slowly, aloud if you can. Do not rush to understand; let the words pass through your ears first. Notice which word or phrase catches. Whatever snags you is the doorway for today.',
    m2Title: 'Meditatio \u2014 Reflect',
    m2: 'Stay with that word and turn it over. What does it call up? Where does it touch your life? You are not after the correct exegesis. The question is not what this passage means, but what it is saying to you as you are now.',
    m3Title: 'Oratio \u2014 Respond',
    m3: 'Say back whatever surfaced \u2014 thanks, questions, protest, pleading all count. This is not performing piety; it is honesty. A reading that provoked no response has not finished yet.',
    m4Title: 'Contemplatio \u2014 Rest',
    m4: 'Stop the words and simply stay. There is no task here and nothing to produce. Most people find this the hardest movement and the most important one: it turns reading from a thing you complete into time you are given.',
    s4: 'How a reading works',
    step1Title: 'Bring a real question',
    step1: 'Not an abstract theological puzzle, but whatever is actually sitting on you: a relationship, a decision, a tiredness.',
    step2Title: 'Receive the passage',
    step2: 'The verses arrive unchosen. This is not drawing lots \u2014 precisely because you did not select them, they have a chance to get around what you already expected to hear.',
    step3Title: 'Read slowly, then again',
    step3: 'Read the surrounding chapter, not only the extracted verse. Notice which word stops you.',
    step4Title: 'Reflect and respond',
    step4: 'Let that word meet your question. Write it, say it, or answer silently \u2014 honest beats correct.',
    step5Title: 'Be quiet for a moment',
    step5: 'Close the text and do nothing. Thirty seconds is enough; ten minutes is better.',
    step6Title: 'Carry one thing out',
    step6: 'A line to remember, a call to make, a grip to loosen. The reflection is finished when it lands back in your life.',
    s5: 'Where the reading lands',
    thArea: 'Life area',
    thImagery: 'Passages that often come',
    thRehearse: 'What the reflection offers',
    row1: ['Work and calling', 'Ecclesiastes 3:1, Philippians 4:13, Proverbs 16:9', 'Discerning a next step inside uncertainty, rather than demanding a guarantee'],
    row2: ['Relationships', '1 Corinthians 13:4-7, Ephesians 4:32, Romans 12:18', 'Seeing your own half of a conflict first'],
    row3: ['Well-being', 'Matthew 11:28, Psalm 23, Isaiah 40:31', 'Letting yourself rest, and saying the tiredness out loud'],
    row4: ['Faith and doubt', 'Psalm 13, Mark 9:24, Romans 8:28', 'Bringing the doubt into the prayer instead of leaving it at the door'],
    s6: 'Why "not divination" matters',
    h1Title: 'Scripture does not predict your future.',
    h1Body: 'Lectio Divina has never claimed to reveal what is going to happen. It does something else: it helps you stand a little more steadily in front of what already has.',
    h2Title: 'Your response is the point of the time.',
    h2Body: 'There is no cipher for an expert to unlock. The passage sits there; what matters is how you answer it \u2014 and nobody can do that part for you.',
    h3Title: 'An old and completely open tradition.',
    h3Body: 'Lectio Divina is fifteen hundred years old, its method is fully public, and anyone can practise it alone. The AI here is only a companion: it helps you ask the question more slowly. It does not hear anything on your behalf.',
    cta: 'The most natural way to feel this practice is to try it. Start with a question that matters \u2014 and treat the passage that arrives as something to sit with, not an answer to collect.',
    ctaButton: 'Begin a reading',
  },
} as const;

const t = copy[lang];
const steps = [
  { title: t.step1Title, body: t.step1 },
  { title: t.step2Title, body: t.step2 },
  { title: t.step3Title, body: t.step3 },
  { title: t.step4Title, body: t.step4 },
  { title: t.step5Title, body: t.step5 },
  { title: t.step6Title, body: t.step6 },
];
const mechanisms = [
  { title: t.m1Title, body: t.m1 },
  { title: t.m2Title, body: t.m2 },
  { title: t.m3Title, body: t.m3 },
  { title: t.m4Title, body: t.m4 },
];
const rows = [t.row1, t.row2, t.row3, t.row4];
const hinge = [
  { title: t.h1Title, body: t.h1Body },
  { title: t.h2Title, body: t.h2Body },
  { title: t.h3Title, body: t.h3Body },
];

// Bilingual FAQ. Answers are grounded in the site's own verified facts:
// pricing.astro (plans/quotas), the lectionary source, and the "not
// divination" statement shared with public/llms.txt.
const faqCopy = {
  zh: {
    heading: '常见问题',
    items: [
      {
        q: '什么是圣言诵读（Lectio Divina）？',
        a: '一种源自六世纪本笃会传统的基督徒祈祷读经方式：缓慢诵读一段简短经文（诵读），反复默想（默想），以祷告回应（祈祷），最后在静默中安息（默观）。',
      },
      {
        q: 'Lectio 是占卜或算命吗？',
        a: '不是。Lectio 从不预言未来，也不提供占卜式解读。经文不预言你的明天；这个练习是带你把真实的问题带到经文面前，并停留在它所唤起的地方。',
      },
      {
        q: '每日经文从哪里来？',
        a: '来自《通用读经表》（Revised Common Lectionary）。每个日历日只有一段经文，所有读者领受的都相同，诵读随教会年历推进，而不随个人口味挑选。',
      },
      {
        q: '开始使用需要注册吗？',
        a: '不需要。访客可以直接开始今日诵读。注册免费账号后，每日次数更多，还可获得更长布局的体验额度，并拥有永不公开的私人日记本。',
      },
      {
        q: 'Lectio 收费多少？',
        a: '访客每日 3 次经文默想，注册用户每日 6 次，另附体验额度（圣言诵读 ×3、深度诵读 ×1）。基础版 $4.99/月，专业版 $11.99/月（全部布局、不限次数）。月付首月免费，年付立省 40%。',
      },
      {
        q: '网站支持中文吗？',
        a: '支持——每个页面都提供中英双语，可通过导航中的语言链接或网址参数 ?lang=zh 切换。',
      },
    ],
  },
  en: {
    heading: 'Frequently asked questions',
    items: [
      {
        q: 'What is Lectio Divina?',
        a: 'An ancient Christian prayer practice handed down from the sixth-century Benedictine tradition. A short passage is read slowly (lectio), reflected on (meditatio), responded to in prayer (oratio), and rested with in silence (contemplatio).',
      },
      {
        q: 'Is Lectio fortune-telling or divination?',
        a: 'No. Lectio never predicts the future and does not offer fortune-telling. Scripture does not predict your tomorrow; the practice helps you bring your real questions to a passage and stay with what it stirs.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Where do the daily passages come from?',
        a: 'From the Revised Common Lectionary. Each calendar day has one short passage, the same for every reader, so the reading follows the church year rather than personal taste.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Do I need an account to begin?',
        a: 'No. Guests can start today\u2019s reading right away. A free account adds more daily readings, trial credits for the longer layouts, and a private journal that is never shared or published.',
      },
      {
        q: 'What does Lectio cost?',
        a: 'Guests get 3 Daily Word readings a day; free accounts get 6, plus trial credits (Lectio Divina \u00d73, Deep Lectio \u00d71). Basic is $4.99/mo and Pro is $11.99/mo with every layout and unlimited readings. The first month is free on monthly plans, and annual billing saves 40%.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Is the site available in Chinese?',
        a: 'Yes \u2014 every page is fully bilingual in English and \u4e2d\u6587. Switch with the language links in the navigation or the ?lang=zh URL parameter.',
      },
    ],
  },
};
const faq = faqCopy[lang];
const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faq.items.map((item) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: item.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: item.a },
  })),
};
---
<Layout title={t.title} description={t.description} lang={lang}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
  <div class="policy-page">
    <div class="policy-head">
      <img src="/logo.webp" alt="Lectio" class="site-logo" width="512" height="512" />
      <h1>{t.title}</h1>
      <p class="policy-updated">{t.tagline}</p>
    </div>

    <p class="policy-intro">{t.intro}</p>

    <section class="policy-section">
      <h2>{t.s1}</h2>
      <p class="dt-thesis">{t.s1body}</p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-section">
      <h2>{t.s2}</h2>
      <div class="dt-grid">
        <div class="dt-card">
          <h3>{t.s2aTitle}</h3>
          <p>{t.s2a}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dt-card">
          <h3>{t.s2bTitle}</h3>
          <p>{t.s2b}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-section">
      <h2>{t.s3}</h2>
      <div class="dt-grid">
        {mechanisms.map((m, i) => (
          <div class="dt-card" id={['lectio', 'meditatio', 'oratio', 'contemplatio'][i]}>
            <h3><span class="dt-num">{i + 1}</span>{m.title}</h3>
            <p>{m.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-section">
      <h2>{t.s4}</h2>
      <ol class="dt-steps">
        {steps.map((s, i) => (
          <li>
            <span class="dt-step-n">{i + 1}</span>
            <div class="dt-step-body">
              <h3>{s.title}</h3>
              <p>{s.body}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-section">
      <h2>{t.s5}</h2>
      <table class="policy-table">
        <tr>
          <th>{t.thArea}</th>
          <th>{t.thImagery}</th>
          <th>{t.thRehearse}</th>
        </tr>
        {rows.map((row) => (
          <tr>
            <td class="dt-area">{row[0]}</td>
            <td>{row[1]}</td>
            <td>{row[2]}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-section">
      <h2>{t.s6}</h2>
      <ul class="dt-hinge">
        {hinge.map((h) => (
          <li><strong>{h.title}</strong> {h.body}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="policy-section" id="faq">
      <h2>{faq.heading}</h2>
      <div class="dt-grid">
        {faq.items.map((item) => (
          <div class="dt-card">
            <h3>{item.q}</h3>
            <p>{item.a}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="upsell-cta">
      <p class="upsell-message">{t.cta}</p>
      <a class="upsell-button" href="/">{t.ctaButton}</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .dt-thesis {
    background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--gold); border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 18px 20px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--text); font-size: 15px;
  }
  .dt-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 14px; }
  .dt-card {
    background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
    border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 18px;
  }
  /* Deep links from the homepage's four path cards land here. */
  .dt-card[id] { scroll-margin-top: 96px; }
  .dt-card h3 { color: var(--gold); font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .dt-card p { color: var(--text); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0; }
  .dt-num {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    width: 22px; height: 22px; border-radius: 50%; margin-right: 8px;
    background: var(--accent); color: #fff; font-size: 12px; vertical-align: 1px;
  }
  .dt-steps { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .dt-steps li { display: flex; gap: 14px; padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--panel-border); }
  .dt-steps li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .dt-step-n {
    flex: 0 0 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--gold); color: #1a1a1a; font-weight: bold; font-size: 14px;
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  }
  .dt-step-body h3 { margin: 2px 0 4px; font-size: 15px; color: var(--text); }
  .dt-step-body p { margin: 0; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-dim); line-height: 1.65; }
  .dt-area { color: var(--gold); }
  .dt-hinge { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .dt-hinge li { position: relative; padding: 8px 0 8px 24px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text); line-height: 1.7; }
  .dt-hinge li::before {
    content: ""; position: absolute; left: 4px; top: 17px;
    width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--gold);
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .dt-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
